A host keeps each folder's extension factories, not one folder's.

pi caches the factories it loads for one folder and empties the cache
whenever a load comes from another, with jiti's module cache off. A host
opens and wakes conversations in many folders, so each open or wake in a
folder other than the last evaluated every extension's modules again: the
host's loop stalled for seconds each time and its memory grew with every
copy. Each folder now keeps its own map. Conversations in one folder share
modules as two opened back to back in it always did, and nothing is shared
across folders. A folder holds its factories weakly and each extension
made from one holds it, so they stay only while a live conversation there
holds its extensions: once the last one there ends or parks they can be
collected, and the next open loads afresh. The sixteen folders loaded
most recently are the ceiling. A reload still empties every folder's map,
and a token keeps its own map, so a load in flight when another folder's
starts still caches what it loads.

